# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable pipeline output (review finding #5).
# The working tree was 24 MB for ~31 KB of code. All of the below is rebuildable
# from the crawl metadata, which IS tracked:
#   python run.py fetch --all && python run.py ocr --all && python run.py index --all
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Vector store (was 15 MB, plus orphaned segment dirs)
chroma_db/
cg/chroma_db/
bihar/chroma_db/

# Downloaded source PDFs
*_all_pdfs/

# Extracted text and machine-translation output
processed_docs.json
translated_docs.json
*/processed_docs.json
*/translated_docs.json

claude_handoff/

# On-demand translation cache (machine-specific, rebuilds itself)
translation_cache.json

# Combined TLS trust stores, rebuilt from the standard roots + a vendored
# intermediate in pipeline/certs/ (see crawler.verify_for). The certificates
# themselves ARE tracked; this is only the generated concatenation.
.cache/

# NOTE: crawl_metadata.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is small, it is the
# record of what was crawled and from where, and it is what lets a fresh clone
# reconstruct its own PDF store.
